# Blueprint System Architecture Rules

## Core Principle: AI is Optional

The system MUST work without AI. AI features are enhancements, not requirements.

### Deterministic Core (No AI)
- File import: .mcstructure, .json, .schematic
- 3D visualization
- Layer-by-layer viewing
- Materials list generation
- Export to all formats
- Minecraft game sync via WebSocket

### Optional AI Features (Can Fail Gracefully)
- Block type identification from screenshots (NOT coordinates)
- Build style analysis
- Similar build suggestions

## Control Flow Rules

### Single Run Controller
All analysis operations MUST go through runController.ts:
- One active run at a time
- New run cancels previous run
- Hard API call limit (25 per run)
- Explicit state machine: idle -> preparing -> analyzing -> complete/failed/cancelled

### No Retry on Zero Results
If AI returns 0 blocks, that is a TERMINAL state. Do not retry.
Zero blocks = honest uncertainty, not a transient error.

### API Call Rules
1. Every API call MUST be recorded via runController.recordApiCall()
2. Calls blocked if run is cancelled or limit exceeded
3. All async operations MUST respect the abort signal

## Failure Categories

Category | Retry | User Message
---------|-------|-------------
user_cancelled | No | Analysis was cancelled.
input_invalid | No | The input file could not be processed.
api_error | Yes once | AI service error. Try again.
api_quota_exceeded | No | Daily limit reached. Try tomorrow.
parse_error | No | AI response could not be understood.
zero_results | No | No blocks detected in the image.
timeout | No | Analysis took too long.

